      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُبْرِدٌ</span></b>  [act. part. n. of 4]. You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جِئْنَاكَ مُبْرِدِينَ</span>
<i>We came to thee when the heat had become allayed.</i>
(T.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also One <i>sending,</i> or <i>who sends, a</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَرِيد</span>
[or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُرُد</span>, i. e., <i>a messenger on a post-mule</i> or <i>posthorse,</i> or <i>messengers on post-mules</i> or <i>post-horses</i>].
(S.)

